 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law and the public authorities law, in relation\nto the chair of the New York state energy research and development authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S8318",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8318-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §169, Exec L; amd §1852, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8318\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would amend section 169 of the executive law and section 1852\nof the public authorities law in relation to the position of chair of\nthe New York State Energy Research and Development Authority\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 1(c) of § 169 of Executive Law (EXC) to\nremove the Chair of the Energy Research and Development Authority from\nthe salary schedule established therein.\n\nSection 2: Amends subdivisions 4 and 5 of § 1852 of Public Authorities\nLaw (PAL) to clarify that the Chair shall not receive a salary and to\nremove language that prevents the Chair of the Authority from engaging\nin private employment. Amends PAL to authorize the Commissioner of the\nDepartment of Environmental Conservation and the Chair of the Public\nService Commission to have outside employment to align with existing\nauthorizations.\n\nSection 3: Provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe referenced provisions are a vestige of when the State Energy Office\n(SEO), an executive agency, existed at the same time as NYSERDA and the\nChair of the SEO served ex-officio as the Chair and CEO of NYSERDA. The\nSEO was disbanded in accordance with Chapter 83 of the laws of 1995,\neffective June 20th, 1995, and all functions were moved to NYSERDA.\nNYSERDA's statute was subsequently amended with a structural change\nseparating the function of Chair and CEO, to make clear that it is the\nPresident that is primarily responsible for the executive and adminis-\ntrative functions of NYSERDA, and that the Chair's role was that of a\nliaison between the Board and NYSERDA Staff.\n\nSince this structural change occurred, the position of NYSERDA's Chair\nbecame an unpaid, volunteer position occupied by an independent person\nwho have been otherwise employed outside state government. In what\nappears to have been an oversight, the provisions at issue in in EXC §\n169 and PAL § 1852 have never been modified to align with the statutory\nstructural shift.\n\nThis bill will remove the now anomalous outside employment restrictions\non the Chair of the Energy Research and Development Authority, to clari-\nfy any ambiguities created from allowing unpaid volunteer outside\nexperts to serve as Chair of the Authority, as has been the practice\nsince the SEO was disbanded as described above.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
